# fixedbugs, defect 559, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C0; the
# critic's `skew32`).
#
# `S` is `{ int a; int b; }` as this module's unit reads
# `fixedbugs-559-skew.h`, and `{ long long a; int b; }` where the other module's
# header has defined `WIDE`, which no unit of this module includes. Until
# 2026-10-10 the probes read every header of the program in one unit, the
# other module's first, so the correct `a: i32` was refused, here as the
# header not compiling at all. It builds now, laid out as its own unit reads
# it.
use fixedbugs559/wide

extern "fixedbugs-559-skew.h"
    record S
        a: i32
        b: i32

function main()
    s = S(a: 1, b: 2)
    print(wide.doubled(x: 3) + to_i64(s.a + s.b).must())
